## Building Fun Robotics Projects Together

The Robotics and Rover Division is a community of university students across Sri Lanka who love building robots, tinkering with electronics, and exploring how rovers work on the Moon and Mars.

Whether you are in your first year of university with zero coding experience or already love building microcontrollers, our division is a welcoming place to learn, make mistakes, and build cool projects with teammates who share your curiosity.

## What We Do in Our Club

### 1. Hands-On Rover Prototyping
We design and build small scale rover models to understand how planetary vehicles move over rocks and sand:
- Learning 3D CAD modeling with beginner friendly tools like Autodesk Fusion 360
- Experimenting with 3D printed parts, laser cut acrylic, and lightweight aluminum frames
- Assembling rocker-bogie wheel suspensions that can climb over small obstacles without flipping

### 2. Electronics, Arduino, and Coding
We teach each other practical electronics through step-by-step club workshops:
- Wiring motor drivers, ultrasonic sensors, and microcontrollers like Arduino, ESP32, and Raspberry Pi
- Getting started with Python and C++ for robot motor control and remote joystick driving
- Exploring the basics of computer vision and webcams to help rovers detect colors and avoid walls

### 3. Robotic Arms and Fun Mechanisms
Members try out creative mechanics to pick up small objects and test sensors:
- Building 3D printed robotic arms with servo motors and simple gearboxes
- Writing basic code to control arm movements and gripper fingers
- Designing small sensor bays that can measure temperature, humidity, and soil moisture

## What You Get as a Student Member

- Friendly Peer Learning: Senior members and alumni help guide beginners with patience. No prior experience is required to join.
- Team Project Experience: Work on fun weekend builds, mini hackathons, and intra-club robotics showcases.
- Multidisciplinary Friends: Meet friendly peers from engineering, IT, physical science, and computer science faculties across Sri Lanka.
